<?xml version="1.0"?>
<robot name="srl_dual" xmlns:xacro="http://ros.org/wiki/xacro">

  <xacro:arg name="use_fake_hardware" default="true"/>
  <!-- Grippers get their OWN flag. robotiq_driver is not built in this
       workspace (the plugin class is not registered), and a missing gripper
       plugin aborts the ENTIRE hardware load including the arms. Keeping the
       grippers mock lets the real ARMS come up on their own. -->
  <xacro:arg name="use_fake_gripper_hardware" default="true"/>
  <!-- PER-ARM hardware selection. kortex_driver exports the Cartesian
       command interfaces (tcp/twist.*, tcp/pose.*) WITHOUT an arm prefix, so
       two real Kortex components collide:
         "ResourceStorage: Tried to insert CommandInterface with already
          existing key. Insert[tcp/twist.linear.x]"
       and the collision aborts the whole hardware load. Until that is fixed
       upstream, only ONE arm may use the real driver at a time. -->
  <xacro:arg name="left_use_fake_hardware"  default="$(arg use_fake_hardware)"/>
  <xacro:arg name="right_use_fake_hardware" default="$(arg use_fake_hardware)"/>
  <xacro:arg name="left_robot_ip"  default="192.168.1.10"/>
  <xacro:arg name="right_robot_ip" default="192.168.1.9"/>
  <!-- Each real gripper needs its OWN serial port. The vendor macro defaults
       both to /dev/ttyUSB0, so with two real arms the two drivers would fight
       over one device: the same unprefixed-resource class of bug as the
       reactivate_gripper GPIO. -->
  <xacro:arg name="left_gripper_com_port"  default="/dev/ttyUSB0"/>
  <xacro:arg name="right_gripper_com_port" default="/dev/ttyUSB1"/>

  <!-- ARM MOUNT. Derived in closed form; see human_backpack.xacro and
       CLAUDE.md. Position is backpack-relative; the backpack link is at
       torso+(0,-0.12,0.02), so world = (mount_x, mount_y-0.12, mount_z+1.07).
       Exposed as arguments so a candidate can be swept without editing. -->
  <xacro:arg name="mount_x" default="0.35"/>
  <xacro:arg name="mount_y" default="-0.2"/>
  <xacro:arg name="mount_z" default="0.18"/>
  <xacro:arg name="left_mount_rpy"  default="1.247666407 -0.232161321 1.769864051"/>
  <xacro:arg name="right_mount_rpy" default="-1.256457931 -0.033197491 1.437832587"/>

  <link name="world"/>

  <xacro:include filename="$(find srl_description)/urdf/human_backpack.xacro"/>
  <xacro:human_backpack parent="world"
                        mount_x="$(arg mount_x)"
                        mount_y="$(arg mount_y)"
                        mount_z="$(arg mount_z)"
                        left_mount_rpy="$(arg left_mount_rpy)"
                        right_mount_rpy="$(arg right_mount_rpy)"/>

  <xacro:include filename="$(find kortex_description)/arms/gen3/7dof/urdf/gen3_macro.xacro"/>
  <!-- Robotiq 2F-85 gripper macro (from the robotiq_description package,
       included via kortex_description's own grippers/ path, matching
       exactly how kortex_robot.xacro's load_robot wires it in). -->
  <xacro:include filename="$(find kortex_description)/grippers/robotiq_2f_85/urdf/robotiq_2f_85_macro.xacro"/>

  <!-- LEFT arm.
       initial_positions == THE MANUALLY SET PICK POSE (set 2026-08-25).
       Kortex 66.57/57.15/127.04/220.83/207.03/239.68/352.51.
       Mirrors config/home_positions_left.txt; KEEP THE TWO IN STEP.
       One updated without the other is a documented trap in this project.

       MEASURED FROM THE HARDWARE, not solved. The operator positioned the
       physical left arm by hand and asked for this pose to be home. Captured
       from /real_status_left - the REAL encoder values published by
       kortex_highlevel_bridge_left - 40 samples, max spread 0.000000 rad.
       Raw capture: recordings/baselines/pick_pose_manual.json.

       IT REPLACES THE SOLVED PRESENTATION POSE (2026-08-16), which is not
       lost: recordings/baselines/home_solved.json holds it with every
       achieved constraint value, and git revision 3d33f8a holds the files.

       WHY IT CHANGED. The presentation pose holds the wrist LEVEL, so the
       gripper camera looks ACROSS THE ROOM. Photographed from the real left
       wrist camera at that pose on 2026-08-25, the frame holds a hoist, a
       lighting truss and the far wall - no table, no cube. This pose is the
       same posture with joint_4 and joint_6 tipped down 44.85 and 55.91 deg,
       and the cube is centred in frame.

       SIM AND REAL NOW AGREE, for the first time in this project. Both are
       at this pose. sim_to_real_bridge.enable() compares the real arm against
       config/home_positions_left.txt, and the comparison now passes rather
       than refusing - because the file was written FROM the arm.

       WEARER CLEARANCE was measured before this was adopted, through the
       same Scorer.clearance_parts the guard uses: moving chain 0.3045 m to
       L-upperarm against a 0.150 m floor. The whole-chain 0.2202 m is the
       immobile mount cap and binds nothing. HARD CONSTRAINT 11.

       This value is baked at LAUNCH, so a colcon build is required before the
       sim arms start here. Text files changed without a rebuild leave the
       arms at the old pose while everything else says otherwise. -->
  <xacro:load_arm
      parent="left_mount"
      prefix="left_"
      dof="7"
      vision="true"
      robot_ip="$(arg left_robot_ip)"
      use_fake_hardware="$(arg left_use_fake_hardware)"
      gripper="robotiq_2f_85"
      gripper_joint_name="left_robotiq_85_left_knuckle_joint"
      use_internal_bus_gripper_comm="true"
      initial_positions="${dict(joint_1=1.156804,joint_2=0.982620,joint_3=2.232276,joint_4=-1.646195,joint_5=-2.683967,joint_6=-1.124167,joint_7=-0.119381)}">
    <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </xacro:load_arm>

  <!-- LEFT gripper: attaches to left_end_effector_link, matching the
       parent="${prefix}${last_arm_link}" pattern kortex_robot.xacro uses -->
  <xacro:load_gripper
      parent="left_end_effector_link"
      prefix="left_"
      com_port="$(arg left_gripper_com_port)"
      use_fake_hardware="$(arg use_fake_gripper_hardware)"
      moveit_active="true"/>

  <!-- RIGHT arm.
       initial_positions == CAPTURED FROM THE REAL ARM (set 2026-08-25).
       Kortex 122.10/307.36/58.67/266.25/160.44/320.42/160.29.
       Mirrors config/home_positions_right.txt; KEEP THE TWO IN STEP.

       THE RIGHT ARM WAS NOT MOVED BY HAND. When the operator set the left arm
       to the pick pose, the right stayed where it was - the solved
       presentation pose. So this is the SAME posture carrying the values the
       HARDWARE reports rather than the ones the solver asked for: joint_3
       differs by 0.887 deg, every other joint by under 0.4.

       THAT DIFFERENCE IS THE POINT. HARD CONSTRAINT 1 says the real arm's
       angles are the ones that count, and until this capture the right arm's
       home had NEVER been read from hardware - the text this replaces said
       so itself. This is the first reading ever taken from the right arm.

       Every continuous joint (1/3/5/7) is inside +/-pi as stored; the
       tightest seam margin is joint_5 at 0.341 rad.

       HOME IS DELIBERATELY ASYMMETRIC NOW. The left arm is tipped to look at
       the table and this one is not, so the mirror residual that the previous
       pose was solved for no longer describes home. The rig could not mirror
       exactly in any case: reflecting the LEFT mount through x = 0 leaves it
       168.00 deg of roll from the RIGHT mount, measured off this file.

       WEARER CLEARANCE, measured before adoption: moving chain 0.4032 m to
       R-upperarm against a 0.150 m floor, unchanged to four decimals from the
       pose it replaces - which is what a sub-degree correction should do and
       is a check on the capture. HARD CONSTRAINT 11. -->
  <xacro:load_arm
      parent="right_mount"
      prefix="right_"
      dof="7"
      vision="true"
      robot_ip="$(arg right_robot_ip)"
      use_fake_hardware="$(arg right_use_fake_hardware)"
      gripper="robotiq_2f_85"
      gripper_joint_name="right_robotiq_85_left_knuckle_joint"
      use_internal_bus_gripper_comm="true"
      initial_positions="${dict(joint_1=2.130174,joint_2=-0.917694,joint_3=1.039518,joint_4=-1.640260,joint_5=2.793923,joint_6=-0.697434,joint_7=2.792003)}">
    <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </xacro:load_arm>

  <!-- RIGHT gripper -->
  <xacro:load_gripper
      parent="right_end_effector_link"
      prefix="right_"
      com_port="$(arg right_gripper_com_port)"
      use_fake_hardware="$(arg use_fake_gripper_hardware)"
      moveit_active="true"/>

</robot>

